---
import PolicySection from "./PolicySection.astro";
import { p, ul } from "./styles";
---

<PolicySection title="Cookies">
  <p class:list={p}>StreakBoard sets only strictly necessary cookies:</p>
  <ul class:list={ul}>
    <li>
      the session cookie (<code>sb-…-auth-token</code>, possibly split into numbered parts) keeps you signed in; it is
      removed when you sign out and otherwise lasts up to 400 days after it was last refreshed;
    </li>
    <li>
      a sign-in check cookie (<code>sb-…-code-verifier</code>) is used during e-mail sign-up and Google sign-in;
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>join_code</code> (7 days) remembers an invite until you sign in, which joins you to its group;
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>auth_email</code> (60 seconds) refills the e-mail field after a failed attempt.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class:list={p}>
    We do not ask for consent, because none of these cookies is used for anything but the service you asked for.
  </p>
  <p class:list={p}>
    If you choose "Not now" on the suggestion to install StreakBoard, your browser keeps a note of it on this device (in
    local storage, as <code>streakboard.install-dismissed</code>), so the suggestion stays hidden; clearing the site's
    data in your browser removes it.
  </p>
  <p class:list={p}>
    StreakBoard also registers a service worker, a small script your browser keeps for this site, so the app can be
    installed on your device and, if you turn on reminders, receive and show them. It stores no pages, data or personal
    information on the device. Removing the app or clearing the site's data in your browser removes it.
  </p>
</PolicySection>
